From: Korri downstream <maintainers@korri.invalid>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WaylandBackend: re-arm vblank timer on discarded frames

In the nested Wayland backend (sway -> gamescope -> game) with the timerfd
vblank path, the vblank timer fires once, disarms itself, and is only
re-armed by CWaylandPlane::Wayland_PresentationFeedback_Presented via
GetVBlankTimer().MarkVBlank(.., true). The Discarded feedback handler only
nudged steamcompmgr and did NOT re-arm.

On a kiosk that hides every other surface for a fullscreen game, the
wlroots/Sway output goes idle (no other damage), so the host stops
presenting gamescope's surface and the last feedback gamescope sees is a
Discard. With no re-arm, the nested vblank never fires again, the game
stops receiving frame callbacks, and the sway -> gamescope -> game chain
deadlocks (game frozen, gamescope idle in poll).

Re-arm the vblank timer on discard exactly as the Presented path does
(using the current time, since a discard carries no presentation
timestamp). This keeps the nested vblank loop self-sustaining regardless
of whether the host presents or discards a given frame. On hardware that
keeps presenting normally this is a no-op change in behaviour.
---
 src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp
@@ -1780,6 +1780,17 @@
     {
         wp_presentation_feedback_destroy( pFeedback );
 
+        // A discarded frame still completes the host compositor's disposition of
+        // this commit, so re-arm the vblank timer exactly as the Presented path
+        // does. Without this, when the host stops presenting our surface (e.g.
+        // the wlroots/Sway output goes idle because nothing else is damaging the
+        // scene -- which happens as soon as the kiosk hides every other surface
+        // for a fullscreen game), the timerfd vblank never re-arms, the nested
+        // game stops receiving frame callbacks, and the whole sway -> gamescope
+        // -> game chain deadlocks. Re-arming on discard keeps the nested vblank
+        // loop self-sustaining.
+        GetVBlankTimer().MarkVBlank( get_time_in_nanos(), true );
+
         // Nudge so that steamcompmgr releases commits.
         nudge_steamcompmgr();
     }
